{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Of every clean beast.</b> Rashi explained: destined to be clean for Israel — we learn from this that Noah studied Torah. And puzzling from what we say in Zevaḥim, chapter פרת חטאת: from where did he know? Any animal that the ark took in was clean; any that the ark did not take in was unclean — thus you learn that he knew only from the ark's taking them in. And some explain that one cannot prove from this that he studied Torah, but rather from the fact that he did not offer a sacrifice upon exiting the ark except from the clean animals. But this too is not convincing, for he understood this from what HaShem, may He be exalted, told him — to bring from them seven. For thus Rashi explained on ויקח מכל הבהמה הטהורה: Noah said, the Holy One, blessed be He, did not command me to bring from these seven except in order to offer sacrifices from them. Therefore it seems to me that Noah did study Torah, as Rashi explained. And what we say in Zevaḥim, 'from where did he know,' does not refer to clean and unclean — for from this nothing would be resolved at all, 'any animal that the ark took in was clean,' since the ark took in unclean animals as well, at least two of each. Unless we explain: any animal that the ark took in more than two was clean. Rather, it refers to the verse מן העוף למינהו, which Rashi explained as: those that clung to their own kind. And regarding this he asked, from where did Noah know? And he answered: any animal that the ark took in was clean — meaning, they clung to their own kind; and any that the ark did not take in was unclean — meaning, they clung to those that were not of their kind. And 'clean' and 'unclean' are relevant to the prohibition of cross-breeding, as it is written: אל תטמאו בהם."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:10.962809017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}